{"abstract":"We systematically investigate the complexity of counting subgraph patterns modulo fixed integers. For example, it is known that the parity of the number of k-matchings can be determined in polynomial time by a simple reduction to the determinant. We generalize this to an nf(t,s)-time algorithm to compute modulo 2t the number of subgraph occurrences of patterns that are s vertices away from being matchings. This shows that the known polynomial-time cases of subgraph detection (Jansen and Marx, SODA 2015) carry over into the setting of counting modulo 2t. Complementing our algorithm, we also give a simple and self-contained proof that counting k-matchings modulo odd integers q is ModqW[1]-complete and prove that counting k-paths modulo 2 is ⊕W[1]-complete, answering an open question by Björklund, Dell, and Husfeldt (ICALP 2015).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Curticapean, Radu-Cristian","Dell, Holger","Husfeldt, Thore"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384405"],"event":{"acronym":"ESA","title":"European Symposium on Algorithms"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Complexity theory","Counting subgraph patterns","Modulo computations","Parameterized complexity","Polynomial time algorithms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modular counting of subgraphs matchings matching splittable graphs and paths","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2021.34","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384405","identifier":[{"id":"85115050589","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d51dcde5-ec04-4d8f-afcb-d15635254bfd"],"keyword":["Complexity theory","Counting subgraph patterns","Modulo computations","Parameterized complexity","Polynomial-time algorithms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-0C430DCB61086314B3D7E9F4C1AE1CBF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2021.34","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86408107/LIPIcs_ESA_2021_34.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Radu-Cristian","key":"curticapeanpau","last":"Curticapean","locid":"53c45a58-4c3c-424c-80a2-c39e733fd7c3","name":"Curticapean, Radu-Cristian","orcid":"0000-0001-7201-9905","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger","key":"dellpau","last":"Dell","locid":"ef9b447a-d6c4-4250-a506-093730db84d6","name":"Dell, Holger","orcid":"0000-0001-8955-0786","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thore","key":"husfeldtpau","last":"Husfeldt","locid":"472021c7-73cc-44ba-a4ef-70cd2bed8601","name":"Husfeldt, Thore","orcid":"0000-0001-9078-4512","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.esa.2021.34","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 29th Annual European Symposium on Algorithms","volume":"204"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115050589"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d51dcde5-ec04-4d8f-afcb-d15635254bfd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modular Counting of Subgraphs: Matchings, Matching-Splittable Graphs, and Paths","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384405","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We study the problem of counting the isomorphic occurrences of a k-vertex pattern graph P as a subgraph in an n-vertex host graph G. Our specific interest is on algorithms for subgraph counting that are sensitive to the maximum degree Delta of the host graph. Assuming that the pattern graph P is connected and admits a vertex balancer of size b, we present an algorithm that counts the occurrences of P in G in O ((2 Delta-2)^{(k+b)/2} 2^{-b} n/(Delta) k^2 log n) time. We define a balancer as a vertex separator of P that can be represented as an intersection of two equal-size vertex subsets, the union of which is the vertex set of P, and both of which induce connected subgraphs of P. A corollary of our main result is that we can count the number of k-vertex paths in an n-vertex graph in O((2 Delta-2)^{floor[k/2]} n k^2 log n) time, which for all moderately dense graphs with Delta <= n^{1/3} improves on the recent breakthrough work of Curticapean, Dell, and Marx [STOC 2017], who show how to count the isomorphic occurrences of a q-edge pattern graph as a subgraph in an n-vertex host graph in time O(q^q n^{0.17q}) for all large enough q. Another recent result of Brand, Dell, and Husfeldt [STOC 2018] shows that k-vertex paths in a bounded-degree graph can be approximately counted in O(4^kn) time. Our result shows that the exact count can be recovered at least as fast for Delta<10. Our algorithm is based on the principle of inclusion and exclusion, and can be viewed as a sparsity-sensitive version of the \"counting in halves\"-approach explored by Björklund, Husfeldt, Kaski, and Koivisto [ESA 2009].","author_count":4,"contributors":["Björklund, Andreas","Husfeldt, Thore","Kaski, Petteri","Koivisto, Mikko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384439"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Sweden"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","Helsinki Institute for Information Technology","Lund University","University of Helsinki"],"keyword":["Inclusion exclusion principle","Isomorphic occurrences","Maximum degree","Subgraph counting","Vertex balancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"counting connected subgraphs with maximum degree aware sieving","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/http://www.dagstuhl.de/dagpub/978-3-95977-094-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384439","identifier":[{"id":"85063676476","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d7509174-d74b-4167-8127-38dca1702ce8"],"keyword":["Inclusion-exclusion principle","Isomorphic occurrences","Maximum degree","Subgraph counting","Vertex balancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-6C2FAEF8DA6F7AC34868E3C83F33CC33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/http://www.dagstuhl.de/dagpub/978-3-95977-094-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83629711/LIPIcs_ISAAC_2018_17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fi","key":"helsinki institute for information technology","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Helsinki Institute for Information Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"björklundpau","last":"Björklund","name":"Björklund, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thore","key":"husfeldtpau","last":"Husfeldt","locid":"472021c7-73cc-44ba-a4ef-70cd2bed8601","name":"Husfeldt, Thore","orcid":"0000-0001-9078-4512","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Petteri","key":"kaskipau","last":"Kaski","name":"Kaski, Petteri","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikko","key":"koivistopau","last":"Koivisto","name":"Koivisto, Mikko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783959770941"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"29th International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation, ISAAC 2018, December 16-19, 2018, Jiaoxi, Yilan, Taiwan.","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063676476"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d7509174-d74b-4167-8127-38dca1702ce8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Counting Connected Subgraphs with Maximum-Degree-Aware Sieving","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384439","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"I summarise the ideals and challenges of implementing an exam in introductory computer programming, and report on a successful implementation in 2018 at ITU. This includes pedagogical, curricular, technical, social, and administrative devisions and experiences that scale to other setting in which a student-owned device is used for individual assessment. The core issue is the difficulty of preventing communication with outside sources using a computer with internet capabilities.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Husfeldt, Thore"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382164"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Student assessment","exam implementation","internet restrictions","introductory computer programming","pedagogical challenges"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"valid scalable authentic on site digital individual assessment of programming skills","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83629849/B1_Husfeldt.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382164","ids":["itu-3cc97c24-72c5-47b7-a746-ca90df98c21a"],"keyword":["exam implementation","internet restrictions","introductory computer programming","pedagogical challenges","student assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C890D3746DD8D92BC0BE8F8E1F9AE0E7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83629849/B1_Husfeldt.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thore","key":"husfeldtpau","last":"Husfeldt","locid":"472021c7-73cc-44ba-a4ef-70cd2bed8601","name":"Husfeldt, Thore","orcid":"0000-0001-9078-4512","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"21","publisher":"Lund University","status":"p","title":"LTHs 10:e Pedagogiska Inspirationskonferens, 6 december 2018"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3cc97c24-72c5-47b7-a746-ca90df98c21a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Valid, scalable, authentic, on-site, digital, individual assessment of programming skills","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382164","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Husfeldt, Thore","Häggström, Olle"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384955"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"om frihet är målet behövs en plan för hur ett samhälle utan arbete ska organiseras","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sydsvenskan.se/2018-11-19/om-frihet-ar-malet-behovs-en-plan-for-hur-ett-samhalle-utan-arbete-ska-organiseras","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384955","ids":["itu-fa8eea64-b703-461c-be99-7faffc769d40"],"lang":"Swedish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-953D27B3619AABA2AA006ABDE49EE632"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sydsvenskan.se/2018-11-19/om-frihet-ar-malet-behovs-en-plan-for-hur-ett-samhalle-utan-arbete-ska-organiseras","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thore","key":"husfeldtpau","last":"Husfeldt","locid":"472021c7-73cc-44ba-a4ef-70cd2bed8601","name":"Husfeldt, Thore","orcid":"0000-0001-9078-4512","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Olle","key":"häggströmpau","last":"Häggström","name":"Häggström, Olle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["11040068"],"newspaper":"Sydsvenska Dagbladet","publisher":"Sydsvenska Dagbladets AB","status":"p","title":"Sydsvenska Dagbladet"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fa8eea64-b703-461c-be99-7faffc769d40"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Om frihet är målet behövs en plan för hur ett samhälle utan arbete ska organiseras","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384955","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Given an undirected graph and two disjoint vertex pairs s1 , t1 and s2 , t2 , the Shortest two disjoint paths problem (S2DP) asks for the minimum total length of two vertex disjoint paths connecting s1 with t1, and s2 with t2, respectively. We show that for cubic planar graphs there are NC algorithms, uniform circuits of polynomial size and polylogarithmic depth, that compute the S2DP and moreover also output the number of such minimum length path pairs. Previously, to the best of our knowledge, no deterministic polynomial time algorithm was known for S2DP in cubic planar graphs with arbitrary placement of the terminals. In contrast, the randomized polynomial time algorithm by Björklund and Husfeldt, ICALP 2014, for general graphs is much slower, is serial in nature, and cannot count the solutions. Our results are built on an approach by Hirai and Namba, Algorithmica 2017, for a general- isation of S2DP, and fast algorithms for counting perfect matchings in planar graphs.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Björklund, Andreas","Husfeldt, Thore"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384639"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Cubic planar graphs","Deterministic polynomial time","NC algorithms","Perfect matchings in planar graphs","Shortest two disjoint paths"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"counting shortest two disjoint paths in cubic planar graphs with an nc algorithm","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2018.19","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384639","identifier":[{"id":"85063688304","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e511a721-6ecb-49b9-a940-c996ef0f8af4"],"keyword":["Cubic planar graphs","Deterministic polynomial time","NC algorithms","Perfect matchings in planar graphs","Shortest two disjoint paths"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-913B3150AD4426F4F5D374F8DA4B6972"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2018.19","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83629740/LIPIcs_ISAAC_2018_19.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"björklundpau","last":"Björklund","name":"Björklund, Andreas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thore","key":"husfeldtpau","last":"Husfeldt","locid":"472021c7-73cc-44ba-a4ef-70cd2bed8601","name":"Husfeldt, Thore","orcid":"0000-0001-9078-4512","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.isaac.2018.19","eisbn":["ISBN 9783959770941"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"29th International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation (ISAAC 2018)","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063688304"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e511a721-6ecb-49b9-a940-c996ef0f8af4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Counting Shortest Two Disjoint Paths in Cubic Planar Graphs with an NC Algorithm","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384639","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We devise an algorithm that approximately computes the number of paths of length k in a given directed graph with n vertices up to a multiplicative error of 1 ± ε. Our algorithm runs in time ε−2 4k(n+m) poly(k). The algorithm is based on associating with each vertex an element in the exterior (or, Grassmann) algebra, called an extensor, and then performing computations in this algebra. This connection to exterior algebra generalizes a number of previous approaches for the longest path problem and is of independent conceptual interest. Using this approach, we also obtain a deterministic 2k·poly(n) time algorithm to find a k-path in a given directed graph that is promised to have few of them. Our results and techniques generalize to the subgraph isomorphism problem when the subgraphs we are looking for have bounded pathwidth. Finally, we also obtain a randomized algorithm to detect k-multilinear terms in a multivariate polynomial given as a general algebraic circuit. To the best of our knowledge, this was previously only known for algebraic circuits not involving negative constants.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brand, Cornelius","Dell, Holger","Husfeldt, Thore"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383879"],"event":{"acronym":"STOC","title":"ACM Symposium on Theory of Computing"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Saarland University"],"keyword":["Exterior Algebra","Graph algorithms","Multivariate Polynomials","Path Counting","Subgraph Isomorphism"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extensor coding","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83633902/1804.09448.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383879","identifier":[{"id":"85049880689","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b36fd584-0dce-4cf2-b49f-80c6ddcb3b91"],"keyword":["Exterior Algebra","Graph Algorithms","Multivariate Polynomials","Path Counting","Subgraph Isomorphism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-53FAF49F787AD61120E68BEEDDB0CF62"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/index.html","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1804.09448.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83633902/1804.09448.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"saarland university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Saarland University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cornelius","key":"brandpau","last":"Brand","name":"Brand, Cornelius","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger","key":"dellpau","last":"Dell","name":"Dell, Holger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thore","key":"husfeldtpau","last":"Husfeldt","locid":"472021c7-73cc-44ba-a4ef-70cd2bed8601","name":"Husfeldt, Thore","orcid":"0000-0001-9078-4512","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3188745.3188902","eisbn":["9781450355599"],"pages":"151","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"STOC 2018","title":"Proceedings of the 50th Annual ACM SIGACT Symposium on Theory of Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b36fd584-0dce-4cf2-b49f-80c6ddcb3b91"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Extensor-coding","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383879","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We reduce the problem of detecting the existence of an object to the problem of computing the parity of the number of objects in question. In particular, when given any non-empty set system, we prove that randomly restricting elements of its ground set makes the size of the restricted set system an odd number with significant probability. When compared to previously known reductions of this type, ours excel in their simplicity: For graph problems, restricting elements of the ground set usually corresponds to simple deletion and contraction operations, which can be encoded efficiently in most problems. We find three applications of our reductions: 1. An exponential-time algorithm: We show how to decide Hamiltonicity in directed n-vertex graphs with running time 1.9999^n provided that the graph has at most 1.0385^n Hamiltonian cycles. We do so by reducing to the algorithm of Björklund and Husfeldt (FOCS 2013) that computes the parity of the number of Hamiltonian cycles in time 1.619^n. 2. A new result in the framework of Cygan et al. (CCC 2012) for analyzing the complexity of NP-hard problems under the Strong Exponential Time Hypothesis: If the parity of the number of Set Covers can be determined in time 1.9999^n, then Set Cover can be decided in the same time. 3. A structural result in parameterized complexity: We define the pa- rameterized complexity class ⊕W[1] and prove that it is at least as hard as W[1] under randomized fpt-reductions with bounded one- sided error; this is analogous to the classical result NP ⊆ RP⊕P by Toda (SICOMP 1991).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Björklund, Andreas","Dell, Holger","Husfeldt, Thore"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382621"],"event":{"acronym":"ICALP","end":"2015-07-10","place":"Kyoto, jp","start":"2015-07-06","title":"The 42nd International Colloquium on Automata, Languages, and Programming","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Saarland University"],"keyword":["Exponential Time Algorithms","Hamiltonicity","Parameterized complexity","Parity Computation","Set System Restrictions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the parity of set systems under random restrictions with applications to exponential time problems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81821968/pbdm.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382621","identifier":[{"id":"84950138716","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5b261d61-818a-4a29-81f5-d9466e9714de"],"keyword":["Exponential-Time Algorithms","Hamiltonicity","Parameterized Complexity","Parity Computation","Set System Restrictions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E8C296B52BF54B332FAA71D74DA20EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81821968/pbdm.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"saarland university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Saarland University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Sci